{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell","id":1026392,"title":"Add \"Blank Arcanum\" to a spell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-04T01:16:42-08:00","id":1026392,"title":"Add \"Blank Arcanum\" to a spell","content":"This may be an obvious question but I would still like to get others opinion on it.<br /> <br /> On spells that have the Add &quot;<i>Blank Arcanum</i>&quot; you still need the base spell I get that, but what I want to know is if it is a combination spell following all of the combination spell rules? If so why bother even adding that to the spells description, you can combine ANY spell with ANY spell by following the combination rules? So it seems redundant to add that to any of the spell descriptions. The only reason that I can think of is to give an especially effective example of that combo, but if they were tight on word count for the book this redundancy seem wasteful.<br /> <br /> Substitute &quot;<i>Blank Arcanum</i>&quot; I only see one spell in the book with this entry and that would be Familiar (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), - Substitute Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. Does that mean that is the only spell that you can substitute one Arcanum for another or can you use Creative Thaumaturgy to accomplish this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T01:44:33-08:00","id":1026401,"title":"","content":"That looks like a typo in your version of the book. The book I have says &quot;Add Death or Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T01:52:31-08:00","id":1026405,"title":"","content":"Bummer I just bought my book from Drivethru 1 month ago","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T02:00:58-08:00","id":1026408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026401#post1026401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That looks like a typo in your version of the book. The book I have says &amp;quot;Add Death or Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine also says Substitute, and it's not a typo going by precedent from 1e and the fact it would make no sense.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the add arcanum thing are examples of conjunctional effects, not of combined spells. Since the arcana were written by different authors and there isn't a clear definition of what a conjunctional spell is in the book (My opinion currently is that it expands the number of viable targets for the spell, for instance adding Death to your Bind Spirit spell allows it bind spirits and ghosts simultaneously without it being a combined spell) the overall use of conjunctional spells seems to be a bit haphazard and sometimes seems to makes no sense. Combined spells are different though and there aren't any examples of that in the book. It's still possible to use a different arcana and creative thaumaturgy to create the spell as it makes sense. Going back to Bind Spirit, you don't need Spirit to cast it if you only want to bind a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T02:08:24-08:00","id":1026412,"title":"","content":"Ok that makes sense, so in a sense at that point you are substituting death for spirit for a Bind Ghost spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T02:27:44-08:00","id":1026418,"title":"","content":"In my last example there? Yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T03:13:01-08:00","id":1026428,"title":"","content":"Think about it that way: they only got, let's pick a random number, 100 spells. These 100 spells had to showcase how to put practices into practice (har har) and how to compose your own magic. They had to cover as many effects as possible, to provide a good matrix for future creations. So if you have a spell that can be just reskinned for another Arcanum, there is no reason to reprint it - you already gave the readers mechanical solution how to do it. Instead of wasting 2 of your 100 spells on copy pasta, it's better to introduce a whole new concept. <br /> This, of course, has upsides and downsides; for example, I'm totally a person who would allow (in fact, I allow and I do it myself) Death-based healing, but as there is no spell for in the book, one table might rule it as ok, and another might find it antithetical to the point of Arcanum. This means that all of the players (or at least, individual players and GM) must be on the same page when it comes to what each Arcanum means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:52:34-08:00","id":1026576,"title":"","content":"Most 'Add Arcanum X for' in final print should be 'Use Arcanum X for', as most of the time you can change viably Mind, Death and Spirit for doing particular thing about goetia, ghosts and spirits, respectively - WITHOUT ANY Arcanum dots spell is written in corebook. Like spell <i>Familiar</i> have version in each of those Arcana, or spell <i>Exorcism</i>. Or not written spells <i>Know Goetia</i> and <i>Know Ghost</i>, that works exactly like <i>Know Spirit</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-04-2017, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:56:11-08:00","id":1026578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026576#post1026576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most 'Add Arcanum X for' in final print should be 'Use Arcanum X for', as most of the time you can change viably Mind, Death and Spirit for doing particular thing about goetia, ghosts and spirits, respectively - WITHOUT ANY Arcanum dots spell is written in corebook. Like spell <i>Familiar</i> have version in each of those Arcana, or spell <i>Exorcism</i>. Or not written spells <i>Know Goetia</i> and <i>Know Ghost</i>, that works exactly like <i>Know Spirit</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think they made it they way they did very deliberately to show what a conjunctional spell actually does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:27:19-08:00","id":1026625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026578#post1026578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I think they made it they way they did very deliberately to show what a conjunctional spell actually does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't a conjuction spell two spells woven together as one not two arcana used for a spell? However I could be wrong there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:33:54-08:00","id":1026630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026625#post1026625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't a conjuction spell two spells woven together as one not two arcana used for a spell? However I could be wrong there.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're thinking Combined Spell. Conjunctional is when you add arcana to a spell to increase its effects. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think the reason for &quot;Substitute Arcana&quot; lies in saving word count. Familar basically acts the same way for pretty much all ephemerals, so why waste the space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:16:46-08:00","id":1026647,"title":"","content":"@MCN ah, I understand. Familiar however having substitute instead of &quot;add&quot; does make it easier for a variety of mages to gain or grant familiars without the restriction of needing spirit 4 as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 01-04-2017, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:24:21-08:00","id":1026651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026647#post1026647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MCN ah, I understand. Familiar however having substitute instead of &amp;quot;add&amp;quot; does make it easier for a variety of mages to gain or grant familiars without the restriction of needing spirit 4 as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spells that say &quot;Add&quot; arcana are just saying that adding the arcana gives the spell an expanded range of targets. If Familiar had said Add Death or Add Mind you could still gain a Familiar with just Death or Mind, it would have meant you could simultaneously turn a ghost and a spirit into a pair of familiars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:32:35-08:00","id":1026654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026651#post1026651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spells that say &quot;Add&quot; arcana are just saying that adding the arcana gives the spell an expanded range of targets. If Familiar had said Add Death or Add Mind you could still gain a Familiar with just Death or Mind, it would have meant you could simultaneously turn a ghost and a spirit into a pair of familiars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but to add the death or mind you would require spirit 4. I am simply saying by having a Spirt4 version, a Death 4 version and a mind 4 version more mages are capable of granting and gaining familiars. If a moros for instance wanted to bind a familiar and the familiar spell had 'add' instead it'd be quite awhile before they got their inferior arcana to 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:47:25-08:00","id":1026656,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2909_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2909\" data-vbnamecard=\"2909\">Mr.F.I.X.</a> You completely misunderstand the purpose of Add Arcana X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-04-2017, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T00:20:37-08:00","id":1026897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026408#post1026408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(My opinion currently is that it expands the number of viable targets for the spell, for instance adding Death to your Bind Spirit spell allows it bind spirits and ghosts simultaneously without it being a combined spell) the overall use of conjunctional spells seems to be a bit haphazard and sometimes seems to makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You don't have to purchase this spell as a Rote or Praxis more than once to use it on a different kind of ephemeral being if you have the necessary rating in both Arcana&quot; seems adequate to the task of explaining why the spells that let you add or subtract Manifestation Conditions are cross-applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T00:30:34-08:00","id":1026899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026392-add-blank-arcanum-to-a-spell?p=1026897#post1026897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You don't have to purchase this spell as a Rote or Praxis more than once to use it on a different kind of ephemeral being if you have the necessary rating in both Arcana&quot; seems adequate to the task of explaining why the spells that let you add or subtract Manifestation Conditions are cross-applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad additional benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T05:34:23-08:00","id":1031543,"title":"","content":"Ok Just so that I have a general consensus here. For most spells that have Add &quot;Blank Arcanum&quot; you could use creative Thaumaturgy to make a spell that uses just the Added Arcanum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:02:01-08:00","id":1031563,"title":"","content":"That would be my assumption, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}